<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Akkadian Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Akkadians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Akkadian Empire was the first known empire in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon of Akkad</a> around the twenty-fourth century BCE. It united the Sumerian city-states and extended its influence over neighbouring regions, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>. It declined amid revolts, invasions and climatic stress such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/4-2-kiloyear-event">4.2-kiloyear event</a>, and was followed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-sumerian-empire">Neo-Sumerian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire.jpg" alt="Akkadian Empire" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Middle_East_topographic_map-blank.svg: Sémhur (talk) derivative work: Zunkir (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Empire_akkad.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
